  "text": {
    "markdown": "## Lisbon vs Prague vs Copenhagen for a May weekend\n\n**Go to Prague.** It is the cheapest by a clear margin at **$515**, and since cost matters most to you, that settles it. **Lisbon** is the runner-up: $160 more buys you the warmest weather of the three. Copenhagen is both the most expensive and the coolest.\n\n| | Lisbon | **Prague** | Copenhagen |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Return flight | $180 | $140 | $210 |\n| Hotel, 3 nights | $360 | $270 | $570 |\n| Food, 3 days | $135 | $105 | $210 |\n| **Total** | **$675** | **$515** | **$990** |\n| Average high in May | 22 °C | 19 °C | 16 °C |\n| Cost rank | 2nd | 1st | 3rd |\n| Weather rank | 1st | 2nd | 3rd |\n\n### How the totals break down\n\n- **Lisbon:** $180 + 3 × $120 + 3 × $45 = **$675**\n- **Prague:** $140 + 3 × $90 + 3 × $35 = **$515**\n- **Copenhagen:** $210 + 3 × $190 + 3 × $70 = **$990**\n\nHotels drive the gap. Copenhagen's three nights alone ($570) cost more than the entire Prague trip.\n\n### Weighing cost against weather\n\n- **Prague** wins on cost and is in the middle on weather. 19 °C is comfortable for walking a city all day.\n- **Lisbon** costs $160 more (about 31%) for 3 °C more warmth and a better chance of sitting outside in the evening. If weather mattered as much as cost to you, Lisbon would edge ahead.\n- **Copenhagen** costs nearly twice as much as Prague and is the coolest, so it loses on both of your criteria.\n\n**Verdict:** Prague, unless the extra warmth is worth $160 to you, in which case Lisbon.\n",
    "validation": {
      "valid": true,
      "checks": [
        "is non-empty Markdown",
        "contains no raw HTML outside code (react-markdown would print it literally)"
      ],
      "errors": [],
      "warnings": []
    }
